      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nope. For better worse, C++ `enum class` types are not implicitly convertible to their underlying type; you have to perform a cast.\n\n* https://stackoverflow.com/q/11421432\n* https://stackoverflow.com/q/55537371\n\nC++ 23 provides [`std::to_underlying`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/to_underlying) for this purpose. But in this case, we want `int` anyway, since that\u0027s what `%d` expects.",
      "parentUuid": "bb7ae1da_0cb58749",
